━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means the Meridian source code, binaries, documentation,
   and all associated files distributed under this license.

   "Protection Period" means ten (10) years from the date each version
   of the Software is first publicly distributed.

   "Individual Use" means use by a single natural person for their own
   projects, whether personal or commercial in nature, where no other
   person accesses, operates, or benefits from the same running instance
   of the Software in a shared or coordinated manner.

   "Competing Use" means making the Software or any substantially similar
   derivative available to third parties as a hosted, managed, or
   cloud-based service, or incorporating the Software into any product
   whose primary purpose substantially replicates Meridian's commercial
   offerings.

   "Team Use" means any deployment, installation, or operation of the
   Software where more than one natural person accesses, connects to,
   or coordinates through the same running instance, regardless of
   whether such use is commercial or non-commercial in nature.

2. INDIVIDUAL USE GRANT (FREE)

   During the Protection Period, permission is granted, free of charge,
   to any individual person to:

   a) Use, copy, modify, and run the Software for their own projects,
      including projects that are commercial in nature, provided such
      use constitutes Individual Use as defined above.

   b) Run the Software in personal CI/CD pipelines, automated workflows,
      and build systems, provided such pipelines are owned and operated
      solely by that individual for their own projects.

   c) Evaluate and experiment with the Software within a commercial
      organization, provided such evaluation is limited to Individual
      Use and does not constitute deployment as shared organizational
      infrastructure.

   d) Distribute unmodified copies of the Software for non-commercial
      purposes, provided this license is retained in full.

3. RESTRICTIONS DURING PROTECTION PERIOD

   The following uses are NOT permitted without a separate written
   commercial license from the copyright holder:

   a) Team Use: Any deployment where more than one person accesses,
      connects to, or coordinates through the same running instance.
      This includes but is not limited to: shared internal tooling,
      team dashboards, organizational infrastructure, and any
      multi-human coordination use case.

   b) Competing Use: Offering the Software or any derivative as a
      hosted, managed, or cloud-based service to third parties. Building
      any product whose primary purpose substantially replicates or
      replaces Meridian's commercial offerings.

   c) Organizational Deployment: Installing or operating the Software
      as shared infrastructure within any company, organization, or
      group, regardless of whether a fee is charged for access.

   d) Redistribution for commercial gain: Selling, sublicensing, or
      distributing the Software or derivatives as part of any commercial
      product or service offering.

4. WHAT IS EXPLICITLY NOT RESTRICTED

   For the avoidance of doubt, the following are permitted under the
   Individual Use Grant above and are NOT restricted by Section 3:

   a) A solo developer using Meridian to coordinate their own AI agents
      across their own sessions and projects.

   b) A solo developer using Meridian in their own CI/CD pipeline to
      automate their own build, test, or deployment workflows.

   c) A developer evaluating Meridian on their own machine within a
      commercial organization, provided no other person accesses that
      instance.

   d) Academic, research, and educational use by individuals.

5. LICENSE CONVERSION

   Upon expiration of the Protection Period for a given version, that
   version of the Software automatically becomes available under the
   Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0),
   with no further action required by any party. This conversion is
   irrevocable. Subsequent versions released after that date may carry
   their own Protection Period under a new MSL-2.0 notice.

6. ATTRIBUTION

   Any permitted use, modification, or redistribution must retain this
   license text, the copyright notice above, and all original attribution
   intact and unmodified.

